  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Thursday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Unseasonably warm temperatures continue\nthis afternoon with highs being several degrees above normal.\nBreezy winds this afternoon with speeds up to 10-15 mph, gusts\n20-25 mph. Tomorrow, strong gusty winds throughout the day with\nwinds up to 20-25 mph, gusts as high as 35-45 mph. Red Flag\nWarning has been issued for all fire zones due to the strong gusty\nwinds in combination with low humidity dropping to as low as 9\npercent. Temperatures expected to start a cooling trend, but still\nbe a few degrees above normal in the upper 80s. \n\nSunday, wind conditions expected to be much lighter with speeds up\nto 10-15 mph, gusts as high as 25-30 mph. Temperatures will be\nseveral degrees below normal across northern Nevada and parts of\ncentral Nevada north of the US-50 corridor, while south of the\nUS-50 corridor still expected to be a few degrees above normal.\nHighs in northern Nevada will be in the upper 60s to 70s, along\nthe US-50 corridor in the 70s, while south of US-50 corridor in\nthe upper 80s. By the evening into overnight hours, cooler\ntemperatures will extend into the rest of central Nevada, with\ntemperatures staying near normal, while northern Nevada will see\ncolder air being several degrees below normal with some areas\nreaching to near freezing.\n\nMonday, wind conditions become light with speeds generally staying\nbelow 10 mph. The cooler temperatures expected to remain across\ncentral and northern Nevada with central Nevada staying at near\nnormal temperatures in the upper 70s to 80s, while northern \nNevada stays a few degrees below normal in the low 70s.\n\nRest of the week, light wind conditions with a gradual warming in\ntemperatures staying near normal in the mid-week, then warming\nback to a few degrees above normal by the end of the week.",
